# Build context of the all-in-one image (Dockerfile at the repository root): it uses frontend/ and control-plane/
# only, so everything else (.claude/, deploy/, docs/, data-plane/, local runtime state) stays out. The patterns
# below apply at every depth: a git-ignored file (bytecode, an env file, a key, a build output) does not show in
# `git status`, yet would otherwise be sent to the builder and could end up in the image.
*
!frontend
!control-plane
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.env*
**/secrets
**/certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.log
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
**/*.test
**/*.exe
**/*.syso
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
control-plane/aegis-control-plane
control-plane/data
frontend/e2e
